# Four Core Medical Database Search Specifications

When constructing or reproducing search strategies, you must strictly adhere to the native syntax of each database:

## 1. PubMed / MEDLINE
- MeSH indexing: `term[MeSH Terms]` or `term[Mesh:NoExp]`
- Free-text: `term[Title/Abstract]` or `term[tiab]`
- Study design filter: Cochrane Highly Sensitive Search Strategy for identifying randomized trials in MEDLINE.
- Execution: Prefer NCBI E-utilities (`esearch`, `esummary`, `efetch`).

## 2. Embase
- Emtree indexing: `'term'/exp` (explosion) or `'term'/de` (non-exploded)
- Free-text: `term:ti,ab,kw`
- Limits: `[humans]/lim`, `[english]/lim`
- Execution: Web REST pagination sequence behind Search History (`pageSize=200`).

## 3. Cochrane Library
- Scope: Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews & CENTRAL (Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials).
- Syntax: `[All Text]`, `[Title, Abstract, Keyword]`.
- Execution: Real advanced search form and results portlet (`validate-advanced-search` + `render_portlet`).

## 4. Web of Science Core Collection
- Syntax: `TS=` (Topic), `TI=` (Title), `SO=` (Publication Source), `PY=` (Year).
- Scope: SCI-EXPANDED, SSCI, A&HCI, ESCI.
- Filters: `DT=(Article OR Review) NOT DT=(Meeting Abstract OR Proceedings Paper)`.
- Execution: Clarivate Starter API (`/v1/documents`).
